ecil 1.2 features=0x0000000a
; C++ (ECIL 1.2, slice S3): the typeinfo objects as the writer streams them for
; typeid of non-polymorphic classes (P; Q : P is a __si_class_type_info), of a
; pointer (P *), of a pointer to a const pointer to const (const Q *const *,
; with the pbase masks), of a pointer to data member and to member function, of
; a polymorphic class and of a fundamental type (an external declaration).
; A g++ and a clang unit (Inputs/s3_typeinfo_host.cpp) compare them with their
; own (names, the runtime classes, the masks, the pointee and context fields).
;   const std::type_info *f3() { return &typeid(P *); }  (and f1..f8)
; RUN: %ecil-asm %s -o %t.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=obj -o %t.o %t.ecil
; RUN: g++ -c %S/Inputs/s3_typeinfo_host.cpp -o %t.host.o
; RUN: g++ %t.host.o %t.o -o %t.exe
; RUN: %t.exe
; RUN: %clang -x c++ -std=c++17 -c %S/Inputs/s3_typeinfo_host.cpp -o %t.hostclang.o
; RUN: g++ %t.hostclang.o %t.o -o %t.clang.exe
; RUN: %t.clang.exe
; RUN: nm %t.o | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SYMS

; SYMS-DAG: V _ZTI1P
; SYMS-DAG: V _ZTI1Q
; SYMS-DAG: V _ZTIP1P
; SYMS-DAG: V _ZTIPKPK1Q
; SYMS-DAG: V _ZTIM1Pi
; SYMS-DAG: V _ZTIM1PFviE
; SYMS-DAG: U _ZTId
